id: syntax/lexical/t6/0001
area: syntax
op: PerformEval
in: str:"`${#!\u000A1}`"
out: error: SyntaxError
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-vm: row T6: `#!` and `-->` right after a substitution's `${`; Broiler.VM answers accepted (`${#!<LF>1}` and `${--><LF>1}` are `1`): each substitution is read by an inner tokenizer whose text starts after `${`, which treats it as a source start; a correction of Broiler.VM (JSD-0083); answered by step 1 of SJL-13.3, Broiler.VM's wide path on the shared syntax library
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-hashbang spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-template-literals
script: eval("`${#!\u000a1}`")
note: correspondence row T6: refused, a hashbang only begins a Script, so #! after a substitution's ${ is no token (a correction of Broiler.VM that step 1 makes)
since: 29

id: syntax/lexical/t6/0002
