since: 29

id: syntax/lexical/t6/0003
area: syntax
op: PerformEval
in: str:"`${\u000A-->\u000A1}`"
out: value: str:"1"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"1"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"1"
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-html-like-comments
script: eval("`${\u000a-->\u000a1}`")
note: catalogue row EG0001; correspondence row T6: accepted, --> after a line terminator inside a substitution is a SingleLineHTMLCloseComment; HTML-like comments are Annex B's (B.1.1), on for scripts in both engines' requests (Broiler.VM's JSD-0083, decision D17, rows T4 and R07; Broiler.JS's docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, the frontend's syntax half, the request's switches), so each engine's expectation is the comment's
since: 29

id: syntax/lexical/t7/0001
area: syntax
op: PerformEval
in: str:"`${1 <!-- }\u000A}`"
out: value: str:"1"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"1"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"1"
divergence.broiler-vm: row T7: the template-end scan and HTML-like comments in a substitution; Broiler.VM answers `${1 <!-- }<LF>}` is `"1\n}"` (a different template, no error): the scan has no arm for `<!--` or `-->`, so a `}` inside one closes the substitution; a correction of Broiler.VM (JSD-0083); answered by step 1 of SJL-13.3, Broiler.VM's wide path on the shared syntax library
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-html-like-comments
script: eval("`${1 <!-- }\u000a}`")
note: catalogue row EG0001; correspondence row T7: accepted, <!-- inside a substitution begins a SingleLineHTMLOpenComment, so the } after it is in the comment (a correction of Broiler.VM that step 1 makes); HTML-like comments are Annex B's (B.1.1), on for scripts in both engines' requests (Broiler.VM's JSD-0083, decision D17, rows T4 and R07; Broiler.JS's docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md, the frontend's syntax half, the request's switches), so each engine's expectation is the comment's
since: 29

id: syntax/lexical/t8/0001
