class: divergence
divergence.broiler-vm: row T8: the template-end scan's regular-expression-or-division guess; Broiler.VM answers `${typeof /}/}` refused 2006 and `${...return /`/...}` refused 2007: after `typeof` and `return` a `/` is division, so a `}` or a backquote in the literal ends the substitution or opens a template (the vectors hold the `}` in a character class, `${typeof /[}]/}`, which needs no Annex B, and the backquote after `return`); a correction of Broiler.VM (JSD-0083); answered by step 1 of SJL-13.3, Broiler.VM's wide path on the shared syntax library
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-literals-regular-expression-literals spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-patterns spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-template-literals
script: `${typeof /[}]/}`
note: correspondence row T8: accepted, a regular expression holding } in a character class after typeof inside a substitution (a correction of Broiler.VM that step 1 makes)
since: 29

