id: syntax/lexical/hashbang/0007
area: syntax
op: PerformEval
in: str:"#!x\u000A1"
out: value: f64:0x3FF0000000000000
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row N26: a hashbang at the start of a strict caller's direct-eval text, `eval('#!x\n1')`; Broiler.JS answers a SyntaxError in a strict caller (the prefix puts the `#` past offset 0) and 1 in a sloppy one; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0083), which lands when the prefix goes (F24); answered by SJL-14, Broiler.JS's cut-over to the shared syntax library, whose corrections.md lists it (decision D45)
