id: syntax/lexical/regexp-delimiting/0046
area: syntax
op: ParseScript
in: str:"var b = 2, g = 3; var x = function () {} /b/g; x"
out: value: f64:0x7FF8000000000000
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row T24b: after a `}` that closes an expression (object literal, function expression); Broiler.JS answers a regular expression where the specification reads a division; the row records P accepted and K refused ("Undefined binary operation RegExLiteral") for a regular expression followed by an operand, and with `;` after it the run completes with the left operand's value, no error; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0083); answered by SJL-14, Broiler.JS's cut-over to the shared syntax library, whose corrections.md lists it (decision D45)
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-literals-regular-expression-literals spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-ecmascript-language-lexical-grammar spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-lexical-and-regexp-grammars
script: var b = 2, g = 3; var x = function () {} /b/g; x
note: correspondence row T24b: accepted, after } of a function expression a / is division
since: 29

