id: syntax/lexical/regexp-delimiting/0050
area: syntax
op: ParseScript
in: str:"async function f() { for await (var x of []) /a/g; } typeof f"
out: value: str:"function"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row T24d: a regular expression after a `for await (...)` head; Broiler.JS answers refused: OpensStatementHead reads division; a correction of both (JSD-0083); answered for Broiler.JS by SJL-14, its cut-over to the shared syntax library, whose corrections.md lists it (decision D45)
divergence.broiler-vm: row T24d: a regular expression after a `for await (...)` head; Broiler.VM answers refused: a head needs if, while, for or with before `(`, so after `await` a `/` is division; a correction of both (JSD-0083); answered for Broiler.VM by step 1 of SJL-13.3, its wide path on the shared syntax library
prov: spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-literals-regular-expression-literals spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-ecmascript-language-lexical-grammar spec:es2026@0248456c#sec-lexical-and-regexp-grammars
script: async function f() { for await (var x of []) /a/g; } typeof f
note: correspondence row T24d: accepted, after a for-await head a / begins a regular expression (a correction of both engines; Broiler.VM's at step 1)
since: 29

id: syntax/lexical/regexp-delimiting/0051
