divergence.broiler-js: row T24f: a division after `await` used as an identifier in a Script; Broiler.JS answers a regular expression, which the parser takes as a binary operator (as T24b); the row records P accepted and K refused for one followed by an operand, and with nothing after it the run completes with `await`'s value, no error; a correction of both (JSD-0083); answered for Broiler.JS by SJL-14, its cut-over to the shared syntax library, whose corrections.md lists it (decision D45)
divergence.broiler-vm: row T24f: a division after `await` used as an identifier in a Script; Broiler.VM answers refused: Await falls to a regular expression; a correction of both (JSD-0083); answered for Broiler.VM by step 1 of SJL-13.3, its wide path on the shared syntax library
